  "description": "Change of use from ground floor laundrette (Sui Generis) to cafe (Class E).",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: \r377.26.01\r377.26.02\r377.26.06\r377.26.07\r377.26.08\r377.26.09\rDesign Statement\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987, or in any provision equivalent to Class E in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification, the development hereby approved shall be used as a Cafe, and for no other purposes within Class E unless otherwise agreed by the Local Planning Authority.\rReason: In the interest of residential amenity, to prevent inappropriate uses and safeguard the safe and free flow of pedestrian and vehicle movement.\r",
    "The development shall not be occupied until details of a refuse strategy which demonstrates that the refuse storage area is within the 30m drag distance stated in Manual for Streets has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the refuse storage provided at the site conforms to Manual for Streets and Enfield Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance at New Developments.\r",
    "The use hereby approved shall only operate between the hours of 07:00 to 19:00 hours everyday including Bank Holidays, and at no other times.\r\rReason: To protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers."
  ],
